# Uploaded files are delivered as data, never as markup the browser runs (015-000-0020).
#
# ── Why this file exists ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# data/files/ lives inside the document root, and the root .htaccess deliberately lets it
# through — that is how a file reaches a client without going past PHP. The consequence is
# that Apache serves whatever is stored there, with the type it derives from the extension.
#
# Without FILE_ALLOWED_TYPES (the default is null), UploadValidator blocks only what the
# SERVER would execute: .php, .phtml, .cgi and their relatives. Markup is not in that list,
# because markup is not executed on the server. It runs in the browser, in this application's
# origin: a user with upload rights stores page.html or an SVG carrying a script, sends the
# link, and the script runs as this site.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy from bootstrap-web.php does not help here. It is a response
# header the application sets, and the application never sees these requests — Apache answers
# them from disk.
#
# ── What is decided here, and what is not ─────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Images and PDFs stay inline. Being able to show a stored image in a browser tab is the
# ordinary use of a file store, and neither type carries script that runs in this origin —
# an <img> is not a document. Markup types are the ones that do, and only those are pushed
# into a download.
#
# nosniff applies to EVERYTHING, not only to markup: without it a browser may decide for
# itself that a .txt with a leading "<html>" is a document, and then the extension list
# above would be beside the point.

<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    Header always set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
</IfModule>

# Everything a browser would parse as a document, and .xml because of XSLT and of SVG stored
# under a generic name. svgz is the gzipped form and parses the same.
<FilesMatch "(?i)\.(html?|xht|xhtml|shtml|svg|svgz|xml|xsl|xslt|mht|mhtml)$">
    <IfModule mod_headers.c>
        Header always set Content-Disposition "attachment"
    </IfModule>

    # The second layer, for a server without mod_headers: a type no browser renders as a
    # document. Not a replacement for the header — a download without a name is worse than
    # one with — but it stops the script from running.
    ForceType application/octet-stream
</FilesMatch>
